  "reason": "Evidence: The image encoder (imagenet_vit_l vs resnet50) showed the largest performance gain (+8.3% acc), and transformer aggregation gave a small additional edge over avgpool (0.7207 vs 0.7150). The current best (config_018) uses scvi_n200 as the RNA encoder, but we have not yet tested whether an alternative learned RNA encoder (scgpt) could improve further while keeping the proven image encoder and aggregation fixed. Question: Does scgpt outperform scvi_n200 as the RNA encoder when paired with imagenet_vit_l and transformer aggregation? This is a clean single-variable comparison against the current best. Why: With 6 experiments remaining, reducing uncertainty on the RNA encoder dimension is critical—if scgpt helps, it opens a new exploitation path; if not, we confirm scvi_n200 is optimal and can pivot to fusion or profile-setting refinements. This is the highest-information experiment available that directly extends the current best configuration."
